{
  "id": "COMPOUND:27653 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "Prejadomycin appears to have a complex relationship with SK-VLB through a series of molecular targets. The evidence suggests that Prejadomycin acts as a target for Cocosamide B, which in turn targets SK-VLB. This pathway is supported by multiple high-scoring connections, with Prejadomycin directly linked to VMRC-LCP and Hepatocyte, both of which are targets of Cocosamide B. The presence of multiple intermediate targets, including VMRC-LCP and Hepatocyte, indicates a potential role for Prejadomycin in modulating signaling pathways that ultimately lead to SK-VLB activation. The overlapping involvement of Cocosamide B in targeting different cellular components suggests a possible mechanism of action involving the regulation of cellular processes that influence SK-VLB function. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Cocosamide B as a central mediator in the interaction between Prejadomycin and SK-VLB, emphasizing the role of this compound in orchestrating downstream effects.",
